Subject: [PATCH] GLORYS reference transports through the sections, on GLORYS's
 own grid; model against GLORYS plot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

analysis/glorys_transports.jl computes GLORYS's daily-mean volume, heat, salt and freshwater transports
through every section of [transports] with the model's own code (section_faces, section_transports of
transports.jl): for each section, an Oceananigans latitude-longitude grid whose cells are GLORYS's 1/12°
cells is built over a box around it, with GLORYS's levels and sea floor (partial bottom cells), and
GLORYS's centred u and v are averaged onto the faces. Same staircase rule, signs, reference values and
formulas as the model, without interpolating GLORYS onto the model grid. Downloads small boxes, once.

plotting/gateway_transports.jl draws the model's online transports against GLORYS's for each section.
This replaces fjp/nested's glorys_gateways_native.jl, which had its own staircase code.

